{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Eat, so is knowledge</b> — [verses 13–14] [This is] a command. The proper form is with kamatz, like רדה, and it also occurs with segol, like ידשנה סלה. And likewise the interpretation: Eat honey and the nectar, for they are sweet to the palate; so too know wisdom, for the sake of your soul that you may live."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:28.369056833Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}